    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "The fix is ready! The issue was in `src/money.js` where prices were being converted to cents using floating-point arithmetic (`Number * 100`), which introduced precision errors for certain values like 39.95.\n\nThe solution converts the price to a fixed 2-decimal string first, then removes the decimal point and parses as an integer \u2014 avoiding floating-point errors entirely. Both `parseEuros()` and `cellCents()` functions were updated.\n\nI've tested it with:\n- 39.95 \u2713 (the problematic price from your error)\n- 12.99 and 10.99 \u2713 (the prices that were already working)\n- Various edge cases like 5, 5.5, and 100.00 \u2713\n\nAll now correctly store as whole cents (3995, 1299, 1099, etc.) in the JSON file. Once you approve the git add command, I'll commit this fix.",
